---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '~/lib/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="A practical explanation of how this static site, theme preference and external links work."><section class="container page-head" style="padding-block:72px 40px"><p class="kicker">Site information</p><h1 class="t-h1">Privacy, plainly.</h1></section><section class="container"><div class="prose-wrap prose"><p>MCP Rack is maintained by <a href={SITE.owner.url}>Alexei Udall</a>. The site does not have accounts, an email signup, advertising scripts or an analytics integration.</p><h2>Your theme preference</h2><p>The light or dark theme choice is stored in your browser's local storage as “theme”. It is not sent to an application server. You can remove it by clearing this site's browser data.</p><h2>Hosting and external services</h2><p>The site is built as static files for GitHub Pages. Hosting providers may process ordinary request information such as IP addresses and browser details. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a> for its practices.</p><p>Package links, documentation links and assistant shortcuts take you to other services. Their own policies apply. Assistant shortcuts include a prepared prompt about this public site; clicking does not give the site access to your assistant account.</p><h2>Suggestions and corrections</h2><p>Suggestions are submitted through GitHub, not stored by a form on this site. GitHub issues are public. Contact the maintainer through the <a href={SITE.repo+'/issues'}>repository</a> for site corrections, or use the contact options on the <a href={SITE.owner.url}>owner's website</a> for private enquiries.</p></div></section></BaseLayout>
